A data platform

The group `Ingest` holds `Collector` and `Kafka`. The group `Serve` holds
`Query API` and `Cache`. The `Collector` writes to `Kafka`, with the label
`write`. `Spark` reads `Kafka` with the label `read`, and writes to the
`Warehouse` with the label `write`. The `Query API` reads the `Warehouse` and
the `Cache`, with the label `read`. We guess that `Spark` also writes to the
`Cache`, with the label `write`. The team `Data` owns `Spark` and the
`Warehouse`, with the key `owner`.
---
Ingest { Collector, Kafka }
Serve { Query API, Cache }
Collector -> Kafka: write
Spark -> Kafka: read
Spark -> Warehouse: write
Query API -> Warehouse, Cache: read
Spark -> Cache: write ?
Spark, Warehouse { owner: Data }
